# Tic-Tac-Toe Enhancement Specifications

## Task: Three User-Friendliness Upgrades

Add three user-friendliness upgrades to tic-tac-toe — clarity, onboarding, forgiveness. No changes to checkWinner, minimax, or the round/series model.

---

### 1) AI "THINKING" TRANSPARENCY

The ~300ms AI delay currently looks identical whether the AI is about to win, block,
or move randomly — players can't tell if the AI is "smart" or just slow.

**Medium/Hard only:**
- During the think-delay, show a subtle indicator on the cell the
  AI is about to pick (a faint pulse/highlight) that resolves into the actual move
  when the delay ends — not a hint for the player's turn, just visual feedback that
  something is being "decided," not stalled.

**Easy AI:**
- No pulse — keep it feeling instant/random, reinforcing that Easy has no
  strategy to visualize.

**Implementation:**
- Implement as a CSS class toggle keyed off the existing isAiTurnNow() + level,
  timed to the existing think-delay constant — no new timing logic.

---

### 2) FIRST-LOSS-TO-HARD-AI SOFTENING (one-time toast)

New players hitting unbeatable Hard AI cold can bounce off feeling cheated.

**Behavior:**
- The FIRST time a player loses (or draws) against Hard AI specifically (lifetime,
  per device), show a one-time dismissible toast on the roundEnd overlay: "Hard AI
  never loses — try Medium to actually win, or keep grinding for draws!"

**Storage:**
- Track via storage.js save (`prefs.seenHardAiToast: false`), bump save version with
  a migration exactly like the existing series-key migration (2026-09-12 pattern) —
  default false on old saves, flips true after first showing, never repeats.
- Does not fire for Easy/Medium losses, does not fire for 2P.

---

### 3) MISÈRE MODE CLARITY

Misère flips the win condition but the round-end overlay and turn indicator use
the same "win" language, which reads as a bug to first-time misère players ("I got
3 in a row, why did I lose?").

**Turn Indicator:**
- When misère is active: turn indicator gets a small persistent tag near it, e.g.
  "Misère: 3 in a row LOSES" (config string, per-locale, same override chain as
  existing copy) — visible the whole round, not just at round-end.

**Round-End Overlay:**
- roundEnd overlay copy for a misère round explicitly names the mechanic instead of
  just flipping "wins"/"loses": e.g. "O made 3 in a row — X wins (misère)!" rather
  than a bare "X wins!" that reads identically to normal mode.
- No logic change: resolveMisere(result) already determines the outcome; this is
  copy-only, sourced from config.js strings.

